WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:13.962
Hi! When writing from a picture, first see who is in it, where they are and what they are doing, then write sentences. Today we'll learn how to write sentences and a short paragraph from pictures.

2
00:00:14.112 --> 00:00:19.146
First ask: who is in the picture? A boy, Mum, two girls.

3
00:00:19.296 --> 00:00:23.490
Then ask: where are they? At the beach, in the kitchen.

4
00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:27.186
What are they doing? Is reading, are playing.

5
00:00:27.336 --> 00:00:32.106
Look at their faces: happy, sad, scared.

6
00:00:32.256 --> 00:00:36.546
One sentence can be: A boy is flying a kite in the park.

7
00:00:36.696 --> 00:00:41.082
Add adjectives to make it lively: a big red kite.

8
00:00:41.232 --> 00:00:46.194
For several pictures, use first, then and finally to keep the order.

9
00:00:46.344 --> 00:00:52.122
Check capitals, punctuation and that the tense stays the same.

10
00:00:52.272 --> 00:00:56.730
Watch out! A few words are not a complete sentence!

11
00:00:56.880 --> 00:01:01.722
A sentence needs who and what they do, with a capital and a full stop.

12
00:01:01.872 --> 00:01:06.690
Write it as: A boy is flying a kite in the park.

13
00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:15.114
Your turn! Which one is a complete sentence? Pause and think.

14
00:01:15.264 --> 00:01:22.290
B has who and what she does, with a capital and a full stop. Did you get it right?

15
00:01:22.440 --> 00:01:30.186
Another one! Which part tells where? Pause and think.

16
00:01:30.336 --> 00:01:35.418
In the pool tells the place. Did you get it right?

17
00:01:35.568 --> 00:01:43.842
Here's another! Which word tells how they feel? Pause and think.

18
00:01:43.992 --> 00:01:48.810
Happy is a feeling. Did you get it right?

19
00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:57.474
Try one more! Which word starts the last picture? Pause and think.

20
00:01:57.624 --> 00:02:03.258
The last picture starts with finally. Did you get it right?

21
00:02:03.408 --> 00:02:11.778
Try one more! Which sentence is more lively? Pause and think.

22
00:02:11.928 --> 00:02:18.210
B has adjectives and says what the dog is doing. Did you get it right?

23
00:02:18.360 --> 00:02:28.074
Try one more! Yesterday we play at the beach. What needs fixing? Pause and think.

24
00:02:28.224 --> 00:02:33.762
Yesterday is the past, so played. Did you get it right?

25
00:02:33.912 --> 00:02:43.146
Try one more! What is the right order of first, then and finally? Pause and think.

26
00:02:43.296 --> 00:02:48.378
First, then, finally. Did you get it right?

27
00:02:48.528 --> 00:02:57.114
Last one! Is a big brown dog a whole sentence? Pause and think.

28
00:02:57.264 --> 00:03:05.345
There is no action. A whole sentence: The big brown dog runs. Did you get it right?

29
00:03:05.495 --> 00:03:13.266
Remember: ask who, where, what and how they feel, then write full sentences joined with first, then and finally.

30
00:03:13.416 --> 00:03:18.689
Find a family photo and write three sentences about it!

